Summary of important user-visible changes for ovolesti.

ovolesti 0.0.2 (unreleased)
===========================

  ** HPolytope.volume has a new signature,
     [VOL, LOGVOL] = volume (P, ALGORITHM, WALK_LEN, ERROR, SEED, RANDOM_WALK),
     and offers volesti's three volume algorithms: 'CB' (cooling balls, the
     new default), 'CG' (cooling Gaussians) and 'SoB' (sequence of balls,
     the only one before).  RANDOM_WALK is 'CDHR', 'RDHR', 'BaW' (ball walk)
     or 'Blrd' (accelerated billiard walk, not with 'CG').  Defaults follow
     the R package: CB uses Blrd, WALK_LEN 1 and ERROR 0.1; CG uses CDHR, 1
     and 0.1; SoB uses CDHR, floor (10 + d/10) and 1.  LOGVOL is the
     logarithm of the volume.  Calls of the old form volume (P, WALK_LEN,
     ERROR, SEED) now raise an error: pass 'SoB' as ALGORITHM to keep the
     old algorithm.

  ** HPolytope.sample and HPolytope.volume now raise an error for an empty,
     flat (no interior) or unbounded polytope.  Previously these crashed the
     whole Octave session or returned meaningless numbers.  The check solves
     two small LPs with Octave's glpk.

  ** HPolytope.sample now checks STARTING_POINT: it must be a real, finite
     vector with one element per dimension, strictly inside the polytope.

  ** SEED must be an integer between 0 and 2^32 - 1; omit it or pass []
     for a clock-seeded generator.  Negative seeds were silently treated as
     unseeded, and fractional or too large seeds were truncated.

  ** WALK_LEN and NUM_POINTS must be integers between 1 and 2^32 - 1, and
     ERROR must be finite.  The HPolytope constructor rejects complex A and b.

  ** Zero rows of A are now ignored (an all-zero row with b < 0 makes the
     polytope empty).

  ** HPolytope.volume no longer returns the volume of the inscribed ball
     for polytopes whose inscribed ball has radius < 1 (e.g. 0.787 instead
     of 1.002 for the box [-0.001, 1]^2).  Fixed in volesti, which is now
     vendored at commit 17186ff.

  ** HPolytope.sample and HPolytope.volume can now be interrupted with
     Ctrl-C.  Errors raised by volesti are reported as Octave errors.

ovolesti 0.0.1 (2026-10-14)
============================

  ** Initial development release.  HPolytope class with uniform sampling
     and volume computation.  Package skeleton; API may change.
